**Low Severity**

<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->
The comment describes `printSettingsCommitHint` as a "one-time hint," but it lacks any deduplication mechanism. During a single `PrePush` call, `doPushBranch` (v1) and up to three `doPushRef` calls via `pushV2Refs` (v2) each independently call `printSettingsCommitHint`. When settings.json is untracked, the identical note prints up to four times in a row, each also spawning a redundant `git ls-files` subprocess. A `sync.Once` or similar guard would match the stated intent.
<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->

